    reflection: "Marriage is hard. Not because you married the wrong person, but because two sinners trying to become one will have friction. But don't give up. Your marriage is worth fighting for. When it's tough, remember why you started. Look at your wedding photos. Recall the promises you made. Choose love again - it's a decision, not just a feeling. Serve your spouse even when they don't deserve it. Communicate honestly, even when it's uncomfortable. Pray together, even when it's awkward. Get counseling before you need it. The enemy wants to destroy your marriage; don't give him a foothold. Fight for it. Fight fair. Fight together, not against each other. A strong marriage doesn't happen by accident; it happens by choice. Every single day. Today, do one thing to serve your spouse without expecting anything in return.",
