    verse: "Start children off on the way they should go, and even when they are old they will not turn from it.",
    reflection: "Parenting is discipleship. You're not just raising good kids; you're raising world-changers for God's kingdom. This happens through intentional spiritual formation: daily prayer, regular Scripture reading, modeling authentic faith, and talking about God in everyday moments. Let your kids see you worship, struggle, repent, and trust God. Don't pretend to have it all together. Show them what real faith looks like in real life. Take them to serve. Let them see you give generously. Discuss God's truth in natural conversations. Pray over them nightly. Speak blessing and identity. Your kids need your presence more than presents, your time more than things. They're watching you, learning from you, becoming like you. What legacy are you establishing? Today, pray with your kids. Tell them one way you saw God work in your life.",
